<ToolPage title="Siding calculator: squares of siding for a house" description="Squares of siding for a house's walls and gables, less doors and windows." h1="Siding calculator" lead="How many squares of siding a house needs." crumb="Siding" path="/siding-calculator/">
  <Calc slot="calculator" tool="siding" />
  <h2 id="how">How the numbers are worked out</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Walls</strong> = distance around the house × wall height to the eaves.</li>
    <li><strong>Gables</strong> are triangles: width × height ÷ 2 each.</li>
    <li>Doors and windows are taken away; a <strong>square</strong> is 100 square feet. Trim and corners are not counted.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2 id="sources">Sources</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Arithmetic on the numbers you enter; no outside figures.</li>
  </ul>
</ToolPage>
